BBUUGGSS
     The llooccaallee concept is inadequate for inter-process communication.  Two
     processes exchanging text, for example over a network, using sockets, in
     shared memory, or even using plain text files always need a protocol-spe‐
     cific way to negotiate the character encoding used.

     The list of supported locales is perpetually incomplete.

